Narrative_AttemptInfluenceMilitaryUnsuccessful=While our attempt to influence the military may have been unsuccessful, they are still mildly interested in our research. **At Game End, each** {icon:s3_weapontoken} **token is worth 1VP.**
Narrative_BeastsWereReal=The beasts were real.
Narrative_ChoiceBetweenSecrecyUnknown=I was called upon to make my choice between secrecy and the unknown.
Narrative_CleansingLiquid_Bloom=After less than a day's passing, the azalea blossoms that once dotted the landscape were in full bloom and the radiant sunlight bathed the valley in a honey glow. The creatures that remained found themselves reformed, though still horrific to behold, and went about clothed in dapper suits and summer dresses with hats that could easily be tipped as a friendly greeting.
Narrative_CleansingLiquid_Introduced=The liquid was introduced at the source of the stream that winded through the hoary gloom enveloping the town of {townname}. Like a glittering oil, it spread downstream, turning the murky waters clear once again with a supernatural effervescence.
Narrative_CleansingLiquid_OrderFled=Those of the Order that refused to submit to the cleansing beauty fled into the hills never to be seen again. The cousins were free once again to be the most unconventional presences within the town, and returned to their labors with no further interruptions.
Narrative_CodeDuelloMatterComplete=As required in the code duello, the matter was now complete, and while personal feelings of injustice may still exist between the parties, this conflict was deemed over.
Narrative_ConservativelyDressedWoman=A conservatively dressed woman shuffling papers in her lap.
Narrative_ConsultedCousins=Given the scientific expertise of the cousins (and possibly with no other stable options), they consulted them in private on this matter, hoping to come to a consensus.
Narrative_Crossroads_Directions=To the north, a thick fog swallowed the moors, the gray mist obscuring the horrors hidden beneath. To the east, the road entered a dark forest of foreboding trees with limbs entangled. To the West, the sky burned a deep red above the rocky mountains, seething with demonic ferocity.
Narrative_Crossroads_ReturnSouth=It was also possible to return south to the village again and see what lurked amongst the cordoned streets and torchlight.
Narrative_Crossroads_Storm=The horses reared as a blinding vein of lightning arced across the tempestuous sky, followed by a thunderous rapport that shook the ground beneath their hooves. The anxious party stood at a crossing in the roadway, trembling as they surveyed their surroundings.
Narrative_DebtRepaymentOffer=The gentlemen were kind enough to offer {gen1creep} II a choice of debt repayment.
Narrative_DecidedTo_Lead=...have decided to 
Narrative_DidNotEncourage=For God's sake, we did not encourage this behavior.
Narrative_DiscoveryFamilyExperimentsJournals=While the discovery of my family's experiments and journals would cement my scientific ambitions for years to come, I had never actually met them. I was too young to remember the disappearance of my brilliant progenitor. To lose a parent and then another to the subsequent dementia that followed was more folly than one child should ever have to bear. I was shielded from this reality, rushed away to Vienna, where I was consumed by my studies until my twenty-first year. It was only at my partner's insistence that I decided to settle my inheritance.
Narrative_DistinguishedGentlemanStage=A distinguished gentleman near the stage; his whiskers well-waxed.
Narrative_DistressedMonarchyMilitaryService=I was admittedly distressed by the Monarchy's insistence upon military service to help quell the uprising. But, as a citizen eager to support my country in any regrettable fashion it required, I willingly offered service, or in the unfortunate case that my affairs elsewise required my attentions, submitted my penalty in full.
Narrative_ErrorExclaim=ERROR!
Narrative_EstateUntouchedVacancyCaretaker=The estate appeared untouched by years of vacancy; recently pruned brambles and ivy adorned the iron gate and the expansive grounds were immaculate. A caretaker of great age and a small housekeeping staff greeted us. Although updating the grounds to the more modern standard of the nearby town would prove a daunting task, the servants’ warm reception allayed our remaining anxieties. Upon discovery of my family's laboratory, what had been planned as a mere visit received an indefinite extension.
Narrative_EthicallyDubiousScienceMemorial=With our brand of ethically dubious science now considered a legitimate classification of study, the city council would like to build a memorial. 
Narrative_ForgeNewPath=With my own destiny determined, I resolved to forge a new path into the future and create my Masterwork.
Narrative_FraternityOrigin_DeeperEvil=The disease had revealed a much deeper evil than the family could have ever expected: An evil ignorance that dwells within the minds of the people. It had not only left the previous generation in shambles, but imbued the townsfolk with a profound, insatiable fear, even as the town returned to relative stability. During the day, the people watched the forests, glimpsing dark shadows flitting between the trees. At night, they steeled themselves against the wailing howls of unseen terrors, dreading that their children would be stolen away from their beds.
Narrative_FraternityOrigin_Emergence=That was until the Fraternity of Hunters, emboldened by the success of their clandestine operations, emerged from the shadows on the night of a blood red moon. They wore long-tail coats of black, burgundy, and dark leather, a wooden cross hanging either from their necks or dangling from their sides. They clutched crossbows, whips, and daggers freshly glimmering with crimson fluid. Their blood-stained attire and steel-eyed gaze evoked the undaunted presence of ones who had peered into the void and returned forever changed.
Narrative_FraternityOrigin_StatedGoal=Their stated goal: to slay every last beast in the land and return those who had unleashed this foul plague back to the depths of hell from whence they came. The Fraternity turned the fear of the populace to their advantage. They fed the superstitions of the people, blaming the sickness and disease on fiendish creatures from the dark.
Narrative_FraternityRevelry=In the evenings, the Fraternity gathered in the former Town Hall and celebrated their political takeover of the small town. Observers could hear their loud revelry echo through the streets late into the night. The townsfolk had no reason to doubt their loyalty as it appeared that their activities kept both sickness and superstitions at bay.
Narrative_FrenzyProposal=The Order suggested a single evening, once every few years, where the town becomes a place to unleash all their frustrations at once. They deemed it the night of "The Frenzy." Citing recent advances in the field of psychology, they suggested that controlled indulgence might alleviate the mania they experience.
Narrative_Gen1Sane_WorkEthic={gen1sane} II's parent had instilled in them a strict work ethic. Their refusal to purchase a summer home at their colleague's insistence, while stressful, had allowed them time to engender this familial connection.
Narrative_GrimRealizationStrengthenedWill=It was this grim realization that strengthened my will. If these craven modernists wanted more, then so be it! I would push the limits of science further than ever before and damn the consequences!
Narrative_GuardMilitaryRegalia=A guard dressed in military regalia near the front door.
Narrative_HunchedFigureBrokenTooth=A hunched figure with a broken front-tooth, observing with mirth from the shadows.
Narrative_IWould_Fragment=I would 
Narrative_ImmortalityInheritance=Claiming an inheritance whilst one's parent still lives on; this foreign concept was decidedly unnerving both for the returning youths and their unaware spouses. However, after the initial shock of encountering a surprisingly spry parent tending to the Estate, the additional help did prove useful.
Narrative_ImmortalityNoSecrets=For those whose parents had chosen a more amenable fate, having no secrets to conceal caused less suspicion during interactions with the local populace.
Narrative_Investigate_A_Arrival=I arrived at the {ba} under cover of darkness. I was ill-suited for such stealthy missions, but I kept my cloak and collar about my neck to conceal my identity in case I was discovered.
Narrative_Investigate_B_Arrival=A thick fog shrouded my approach on the cool night that I chose to investigate the {bb}. I asked the carriage driver to await my return on the outskirts of town, while I stole away into the empty streets. Nary a soul was about on this evening, and I was soon inside without arousing suspicion.
Narrative_Investigate_ExposeOrConceal=I could either provide evidence to help **expose** the secret inner workings of the building or I could **conceal** the truth and allow the work to continue. **The decision was clear to me:**
Narrative_LeaveYourMark=Be sure to leave your mark on the world.
Narrative_Letter_EntrepreneurApprehension=Being an entrepreneur myself, in a fashion, these goals are not so misaligned with my own. My apprehensions are only related to how your actions will impact my ability to advance my scientific studies most generously.
Narrative_Letter_FraternityIntentExploitative=amusingly exploitative. The Fraternity hopes to use the recent epidemic as a cover for their activities to unearth ancient, supernatural secrets in the region and use them for monetary and political gain. Although I remain skeptical, if these labors are successful, I will be deeply interested in the results. You only asked for your work to remain **concealed**.
Narrative_Letter_FraternityIntentGood=good. It was astute for you to note how oddly silent the town has remained over the last few years. Keeping a watchful eye over the proceedings, the Fraternity appears only concerned with rooting out who or what is behind this veil of secrecy. You've urged me to **investigate** the secret workings soon to become apparent.
Narrative_Letter_FraternityMeeting=I, {meet}, am writing this letter to you after my meeting with an associate of the International Fraternity of Hunters. Our secret conversation over brunch was quite revealing, and the resulting knowledge has piqued my interests.
Narrative_Letter_HubertusIntentNefarious=nefarious. The malevolent Order is consumed with greed, seeking to unearth the ancient secrets in this area and use this power to alter humanity and spread a plague of monstrous entities across the world. You only asked for your work to remain **concealed**.
Narrative_Letter_HubertusIntentPositive=demonstrably positive. The Order is only concerned with establishing a safe haven for those afflicted by disease. Your representative even revealed a physical peculiarity that had elongated her cuspids into sharp points. She left swiftly before nightfall, ignoring my pleas for her to remain, but she urged me to **investigate** the secret workings soon to become apparent.
Narrative_Letter_HubertusMeeting=I, {meet}, am writing this letter to you after my meeting with an associate of the International Order of St. Hubertus. Our conversation was brief, but the resulting knowledge has piqued my curiosities.
Narrative_Letter_IntentionsLead=It has been revealed to me that your intentions are 
Narrative_Letter_OccultFamiliarity=Being intimately familiar with matters of the occult, this admission is unsurprising. My apprehensions are only related to how your actions will impact my ability to advance my scientific studies most generously.
Narrative_MasterworkCreation_Lightning=Upon the stroke of midnight, lightning struck metal, sending a terrible electrical current through the machinery. My creation awoke, and with wild eyes gazed upon me, its creator. I had done it! I had created life!
Narrative_MasterworkCreation_Weapon=I seized the firing mechanism and squeezed the polished metal trigger. When the dust settled and my laboratory wall had been made to crumble into dust, I was unable to contain a sinister grin. The world would remember this day and the weapon I had wrought. My fame would be legendary.
Narrative_MasterworkExclaim_GloriousCreation=My Glorious Creation
Narrative_MasterworkExclaim_GloryForever=The Glory is Mine Forever!
Narrative_MasterworkExclaim_Impossible=I Have Done the Impossible
Narrative_MasterworkExclaim_Laugh=AH HA HA HAAAAA!!!
Narrative_MasterworkExclaim_LegacyEnsured=My Legacy is Ensured
Narrative_MasterworkExclaim_WorkDone=The Work is Done
Narrative_MoldyLeatheryStenchTown=We were immediately accosted by a moldy leathery stench that festered in our nostrils like burning sulfur from the tip of a match. The air was hot, the entire town deserted as if it had never existed. We were surprised to find our estates left relatively untouched, though palm trees and jungle vines now covered the exterior gardens.
Narrative_MonsterSpawn_Flavor=The Town Hall of the village has been transformed into the unofficial headquarters of the Order. When a player visits the Monster Spawn, they may **Perform an Experiment**.
Narrative_NoFormalResponse_Stables=There was no formal response to any letters expressing doubt. However, an individual at the Stables who could observe the comings and goings of travelers would later provide ways to contact them if the need arose.
Narrative_OnlyOneReleaseSchematicsGlory=However, if I were the **only one** to release the time machine schematics, I would receive extra glory. This choice would definitely cause a completely random special event to occur. It might be really good, really terrible, or somewhere in between.
Narrative_RelayEvents_Solemn=I will attempt to relay the events as they were explained to me, though I fully understand the solemn repercussions of the unfathomable knowledge contained within this text.
Narrative_ScientificWorldNotices=The scientific world has finally taken notice of {townname} and its {playtxt} ingenious scholars. The absurdity of it all! Not only does this hamper their ability to experiment freely, it also gives their work mainstream merit.
Narrative_SevereConsternationScientificEnlightenment=This caused me severe consternation. Was this not what I wanted — a clear path towards scientific enlightenment and support of my family's landmark ideas? Why did their lack of friction vex me so? Did they view my illustrious work as trivial? 
Narrative_SkyCrimsonGlowEstate=The sky cast a crimson glow upon the stone walls of my estate. I felt the air crackle with energy once again.
Narrative_SomberElderlyWoman=A somber elderly woman sitting amongst the crowd.
Narrative_SpiritedGroupCitizens=A spirited group of concerned citizens.
Narrative_SundayAfternoonRousedByRiflemen=On a Sunday afternoon, I was roused from my convalescence by my caretaker. A group of three armed riflemen stood outside my door and had refused my wishes to be left to my solitude. They asked me several curious questions about my national allegiances.
Narrative_TooLongIgnoredSabotage=For too long I had been ignored! One might ask what accursed schemes would push one towards the illicit undertaking of sabotage? I ask, is it not enough to feel forgotten, downtrodden, unloved, and spited by those who would in the same breath speak of you as a colleague?
Narrative_TownJovialModernSociety=Everyone in the town was extremely jovial and greeted us with wide-eyed enthusiasm. The modern society stunned us with its glass buildings, bronze fixtures, and steel architecture. However, the hissing whirr of a steam-powered device suddenly broke the illusion. Along every street corner was a mechanical contraption that swiveled, seemingly following our every move. We felt a unique tension in the air, as if our every move was being watched and criticized.
Narrative_UnconstrainedImagination=I was no longer constrained by the fickle whims of my ancestors. I could allow my imagination to run wild with possibilities! Within moments, I set to creating something new and magnificent - something that would cause the scientific world to quiver in awestruck wonder.
Narrative_UnderwaterVillageInsects=We arrived at an astonishing underwater village. The sturdy glass fixtures surrounding the village created a pressurized chamber that kept the floating phosphorescent sea creatures from entering. We marveled at the engineering required to create such a brilliant enclosure and even considered staying until we realized that all the townsfolk were eating insects by flinging their sticky tongues into the air.
Narrative_VillageRuinMossyFloor=While some of the village lay in ruin, a deep green moss covered most of it, giving the stone a calming natural quality. In fact, the entire town seemed to be seething with this growing mossy floor while the townspeople seemed eerily serene. Patches of moss grew on the skin of passersby, and it all seemed to emanate from a golden statue at the center of the **Park**.
Narrative_WelcomeToMyFathersWork=Welcome to _My Father's Work_,
Narrative_WelcomeToMyFathersWork_Fragment=Welcome to My Father's Work, 
Narrative_WorldChangedUnfinishedPage=The world has changed again and we get the impression that the author of this game hasn't written the description for this part and probably never will. In fact, he specifically requested the page be intentionally unfinished a full year before writing anything here. If you've flipped through the pages of the Village Chronicle, you were probably confused by this page already.
